1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,080
Gloss App is the macOS app for gloss.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,780
It is where you read a package through its interface, day to day.

3
00:00:07,506 --> 00:00:09,426
The window has three panes.

4
00:00:09,686 --> 00:00:10,886
A list on the left.

5
00:00:11,106 --> 00:00:13,606
The details of whatever is selected in the middle.

6
00:00:13,886 --> 00:00:15,306
And a map on the right.

7
00:00:15,996 --> 00:00:20,096
The details and the map sit under a bar of tabs, as they do in Xcode.

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,440
One object holds what is open.

9
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:26,540
It is called Workspace.

10
00:00:27,290 --> 00:00:33,330
It remembers the folder, the reading of that folder, the selection, and the comparison with a

11
00:00:33,330 --> 00:00:33,590
base.

12
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,240
It makes no decisions about what to show.

13
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:39,080
Those come from the same arrangement the page uses.

14
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:42,640
So the app and the page never disagree about the system.

15
00:00:44,667 --> 00:00:46,527
The map moves like a canvas.

16
00:00:46,867 --> 00:00:48,907
The mouse wheel zooms toward the pointer.

17
00:00:49,387 --> 00:00:51,187
Dragging with the right button pans.

18
00:00:51,487 --> 00:00:54,327
The left button is left free to click and select.

19
00:00:55,077 --> 00:00:58,417
The text in the details can be made bigger or smaller.

20
00:00:58,777 --> 00:01:02,737
There are seven steps, from a little smaller to twice as big.

21
00:01:02,997 --> 00:01:06,337
The second is the size macOS itself uses.

22
00:01:07,087 --> 00:01:10,247
You choose a step in Settings, or from the View menu.

23
00:01:10,607 --> 00:01:13,207
The list and the map keep their sizes.

24
00:01:15,233 --> 00:01:16,953
The app also reads changes.

25
00:01:17,253 --> 00:01:20,773
Compare against a base, and the changes page shows what is new,

26
00:01:20,993 --> 00:01:23,113
what moved, and what changed inside.

27
00:01:23,863 --> 00:01:27,403
A change story appears on the page of each type it explains:

28
00:01:27,663 --> 00:01:30,383
each theme, with its title over its prose.

29
00:01:31,013 --> 00:01:36,293
And for every way a change reaches a type, a reach row gives one line,

30
00:01:36,473 --> 00:01:37,373
then the reason.

31
00:01:37,733 --> 00:01:40,373
The rest stays folded until you ask.
